-- DB update 2026_09_10_03 -> 2026_09_10_04
-- Arcane Mage rework, Phase 2 (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md), Rows 4-6.
--
-- Data-only talents per .claude/skills/class-rework/SKILL.md Phase 2: Spell Power, Arcane
-- Barrage, Improved Blink, Arcane Mind (Row 4); Missile Barrage, Arcane Instability, Arcane
-- Potency (Row 5); Arcane Empowerment, Arcane Power, Incanter's Absorption (Row 6). See each
-- spell's `notes`/comment in apps/dbc-tools/source/spells/mage_talents.csv and
-- source/talents/mage.yaml for its own rationale, and the design doc's "Phase 2/3
-- Implementation Notes" section for the full slot-mapping table and the Deferred-to-Phase-3
-- list (this batch adds Missile Barrage's trigger-spell list to that list - it's entirely
-- hardcoded in spell_mage_missile_barrage::CheckProc, not DBC classmask data).
--
-- Talent tab (81/Arcane) slot reuse this batch: Spell Power (1826) and Missile Barrage (2209)
-- move in from their old stock coordinates; Improved Blink (1724) moves within row 4 to make
-- room. Arcane Barrage (86, ex-Presence of Mind) is repointed onto the real stock Arcane
-- Barrage spell (44425, left untouched - already matches the design's numbers). Prismatic
-- Cloak (1726) is pushed forward to its eventual (8,0) new-tree slot, position-only, just to
-- correctly vacate (5,0) for Missile Barrage - removing its source entry instead would NOT
-- have blanked the slot (the build merges source deltas onto the base client DBC, so an absent
-- entry lets the real stock talent pass through unchanged rather than disappearing - see the
-- design doc's Progress notes for this batch). The old (10,1) Arcane Barrage capstone (talent
-- id 1847) is deliberately left untouched for the same reason, pending Row 7-10's Arcane
-- Overload. Arcane Mind's real spell rows (11232/12500-12503) were pulled this batch (had
-- landed in source/spells/generic.csv via auto-detect, moved into mage_talents.csv).
--
-- Produced by `python3 apps/dbc-tools/generate.py` from apps/dbc-tools/source/{spells,talents}/*,
-- then hand-extracted to just the rows this batch owns (same discipline as Phase 1 and the
-- Rows 0-3 migration).
--
-- Regenerate/extend via: python3 apps/dbc-tools/generate.py (see apps/dbc-tools/README.md)

